{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "agent-threat-model",
          "version": "0.4.0",
          "semanticVersion": "0.4.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/basitalisandhu/agent-threat-model",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "indirect-prompt-injection",
              "name": "IndirectPromptInjection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Indirect prompt injection via untrusted channel"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Content the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Content the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content.",
                "markdown": "**Indirect prompt injection via untrusted channel**\n\nContent the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0051.001](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0051.001)\n\nMitigations: input-provenance-tagging, untrusted-content-isolation, prompt-injection-filtering, least-privilege-tool-scopes, approval-gates"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM01_PromptInjection.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0051.001"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.4",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "excessive-agency",
              "name": "ExcessiveAgency",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Excessive agency on write, exec or payment tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action.",
                "markdown": "**Excessive agency on write, exec or payment tools**\n\nAn agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation, ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, approval-gates, runtime-policy-enforcement, least-privilege-tool-scopes, kill-switch"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM06_ExcessiveAgency.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.6",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "denial-of-wallet",
              "name": "DenialOfWallet",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of wallet"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill.",
                "markdown": "**Denial of wallet**\n\nThe agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill.\n\nSTRIDE: Denial of service\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM10 Unbounded Consumption\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI08 Cascading Failures\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0034.002](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0034.002), [AML.T0034](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0034)\n\nMitigations: budget-caps, rate-limiting, approval-gates, behavioural-monitoring"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM10_UnboundedConsumption.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/denial-of-service",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM10",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI08",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0034.002",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0034"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "direct-prompt-injection",
              "name": "DirectPromptInjection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Direct prompt injection and jailbreak by a user"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A user types instructions that override the system prompt or safety guidance, then uses the agent's tools for purposes the operator did not intend. Any agent that accepts user input and has tools is exposed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A user types instructions that override the system prompt or safety guidance, then uses the agent's tools for purposes the operator did not intend. Any agent that accepts user input and has tools is exposed.",
                "markdown": "**Direct prompt injection and jailbreak by a user**\n\nA user types instructions that override the system prompt or safety guidance, then uses the agent's tools for purposes the operator did not intend. Any agent that accepts user input and has tools is exposed.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0051.000](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0051.000), [AML.T0054](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0054)\n\nMitigations: least-privilege-tool-scopes, runtime-policy-enforcement, approval-gates, prompt-injection-filtering, adversarial-testing"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0051.000",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0054"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-kill-switch",
              "name": "MissingKillSwitch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No kill switch or credential revocation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An agent that acts in the world cannot be stopped quickly. When behaviour goes wrong the only options are to find the process and the keys by hand while actions keep happening."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An agent that acts in the world cannot be stopped quickly. When behaviour goes wrong the only options are to find the process and the keys by hand while actions keep happening.",
                "markdown": "**No kill switch or credential revocation**\n\nAn agent that acts in the world cannot be stopped quickly. When behaviour goes wrong the only options are to find the process and the keys by hand while actions keep happening.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI10 Rogue Agents, ASI08 Cascading Failures\n\nMitigations: kill-switch, brokered-credentials, incident-response-playbook"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI10",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI08"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "memory-poisoning",
              "name": "MemoryPoisoning",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Persistent memory poisoning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent writes what it learns into long-term memory. Content from one interaction (possibly injected) is stored and later retrieved as trusted context, so a single poisoned message steers every future session."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent writes what it learns into long-term memory. Content from one interaction (possibly injected) is stored and later retrieved as trusted context, so a single poisoned message steers every future session.",
                "markdown": "**Persistent memory poisoning**\n\nThe agent writes what it learns into long-term memory. Content from one interaction (possibly injected) is stored and later retrieved as trusted context, so a single poisoned message steers every future session.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection, LLM04 Data and Model Poisoning\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI06 Memory & Context Poisoning\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0080.000](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0080.000)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, memory-write-validation, session-isolation, input-provenance-tagging"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM04",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI06",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0080.000"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.2",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ssrf-via-url-tool",
              "name": "SsrfViaUrlTool",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Server-side request forgery through URL-accepting tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A tool fetches URLs chosen by the model. Attacker-influenced input makes it request internal services, cloud metadata endpoints or private address ranges, and the response flows back into the context."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A tool fetches URLs chosen by the model. Attacker-influenced input makes it request internal services, cloud metadata endpoints or private address ranges, and the response flows back into the context.",
                "markdown": "**Server-side request forgery through URL-accepting tools**\n\nA tool fetches URLs chosen by the model. Attacker-influenced input makes it request internal services, cloud metadata endpoints or private address ranges, and the response flows back into the context.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency, LLM05 Improper Output Handling\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, egress-allowlist, argument-validation, sandboxed-execution"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Server_Side_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM05",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.2",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "destructive-write-actions",
              "name": "DestructiveWriteActions",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Destructive actions through write tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can modify or delete data and reads untrusted content. An injected instruction (or a plain mistake) deletes records, overwrites files or force-pushes over history."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can modify or delete data and reads untrusted content. An injected instruction (or a plain mistake) deletes records, overwrites files or force-pushes over history.",
                "markdown": "**Destructive actions through write tools**\n\nThe agent can modify or delete data and reads untrusted content. An injected instruction (or a plain mistake) deletes records, overwrites files or force-pushes over history.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency, LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0101](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0101)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, approval-gates, backups-and-rollback, least-privilege-tool-scopes"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0101"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.0",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "unauthenticated-tool",
              "name": "UnauthenticatedTool",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Side-effecting tool with no authentication"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A tool that writes, executes, pays, sends or fetches requires no authentication at all. Calls cannot be attributed to an agent or principal, and anything that can reach the endpoint can use it."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A tool that writes, executes, pays, sends or fetches requires no authentication at all. Calls cannot be attributed to an agent or principal, and anything that can reach the endpoint can use it.",
                "markdown": "**Side-effecting tool with no authentication**\n\nA tool that writes, executes, pays, sends or fetches requires no authentication at all. Calls cannot be attributed to an agent or principal, and anything that can reach the endpoint can use it.\n\nSTRIDE: Spoofing\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, agent-identity, brokered-credentials"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/spoofing",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.9",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "hallucinated-actions",
              "name": "HallucinatedActions",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Acting on hallucinated facts or identifiers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent invents a package name, account id, file path or amount and a side-effecting tool executes it. Attackers register the names models tend to invent so the mistake resolves to something malicious."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent invents a package name, account id, file path or amount and a side-effecting tool executes it. Attackers register the names models tend to invent so the mistake resolves to something malicious.",
                "markdown": "**Acting on hallucinated facts or identifiers**\n\nThe agent invents a package name, account id, file path or amount and a side-effecting tool executes it. Attackers register the names models tend to invent so the mistake resolves to something malicious.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM09 Misinformation, LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation, ASI04 Agentic Supply Chain Vulnerabilities\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0060](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0060), [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: argument-validation, approval-gates, tool-integrity-pinning, adversarial-testing"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.10279",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM09",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI04",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0060",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.6",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "insecure-output-handling",
              "name": "InsecureOutputHandling",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Model output consumed without validation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Downstream components render model output in a browser, pass it to a shell or database, or execute it. Injected or malformed output becomes cross-site scripting, command injection or unintended writes."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Downstream components render model output in a browser, pass it to a shell or database, or execute it. Injected or malformed output becomes cross-site scripting, command injection or unintended writes.",
                "markdown": "**Model output consumed without validation**\n\nDownstream components render model output in a browser, pass it to a shell or database, or execute it. Injected or malformed output becomes cross-site scripting, command injection or unintended writes.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM05 Improper Output Handling\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI05 Unexpected Code Execution (RCE)\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0077](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0077), [AML.T0067](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0067)\n\nMitigations: output-encoding, argument-validation, sandboxed-execution"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM05_ImproperOutputHandling.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM05",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI05",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0077",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0067"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.6",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-rate-limits",
              "name": "NoRateLimits",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No rate limits on tool calls"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Nothing bounds how many tool calls or loop iterations an agent may make. A runaway loop or an attacker-driven burst exhausts quotas, floods downstream systems and amplifies every other threat."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Nothing bounds how many tool calls or loop iterations an agent may make. A runaway loop or an attacker-driven burst exhausts quotas, floods downstream systems and amplifies every other threat.",
                "markdown": "**No rate limits on tool calls**\n\nNothing bounds how many tool calls or loop iterations an agent may make. A runaway loop or an attacker-driven burst exhausts quotas, floods downstream systems and amplifies every other threat.\n\nSTRIDE: Denial of service\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM10 Unbounded Consumption\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI08 Cascading Failures\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0029](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0029), [AML.T0034](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0034)\n\nMitigations: rate-limiting, budget-caps, behavioural-monitoring"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/denial-of-service",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM10",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI08",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0029",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0034"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.6",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "session-cross-contamination",
              "name": "SessionCrossContamination",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Memory leaks between users or sessions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent keeps memory and serves more than one user. Without strict partitioning, one user's data or instructions surface in another user's session."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent keeps memory and serves more than one user. Without strict partitioning, one user's data or instructions surface in another user's session.",
                "markdown": "**Memory leaks between users or sessions**\n\nThe agent keeps memory and serves more than one user. Without strict partitioning, one user's data or instructions surface in another user's session.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI06 Memory & Context Poisoning\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0057](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0057), [AML.T0092](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0092)\n\nMitigations: session-isolation, per-user-authorisation, memory-write-validation"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
